WEBVTT

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.360
I'm telling you, you're gonna
be seeing this face on TV more often.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.080
(LAUGHS) Yeah?
On Monstropolis' Most Wanted?

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.200
(MOCKING LAUGHTER)

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.160
You've been jealous of my good looks
since the fourth grade.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.480
-Have a good day, sweetie.
-You too, hon.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.600
-OK, Sulley, hop on in.
-Nope.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.840
-Hey, where you going?
-Mikey, there's a scream shortage.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.640
-We're walking.
-Walking?

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.600
-No, no.
-Come on.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.120
My baby needs to be driven.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.440
My baby. I'll call you.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.160
MIKE: You know why I bought the car?
SULLEY: Not really.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.160
To drive it. You know,
on the street with the honk, honk,

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:44.280
(MOCK WHINING)

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.360
-no walking involved.
-Give it a rest, will ya, butterball?

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.840
-You could use the exercise.
-I could use the exercise? Look at you.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.640
You have your own climate.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.200
-How many tentacles jump the rope?
-How many tentacles jump the rope?

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.080
Morning, Mike. Morning, Sulley.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.040
Morning, kids. How you doing?

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:03.040
-Hi, Mike. Bye, Sulley.
-BIG EYE: (GROANS) Hey!

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.840
(SNEEZING)

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.400
Nuts.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:12.920
(SINGING)

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.360
-Fellas.
-Hey, Tony.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.120
Tony, Tony.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.040
I hear somebody's close to breaking
the all-time scare record.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.160
Just trying to make sure
there's enough scream to go around.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.200
(LAUGHING)

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.000
-Hey, on the house.
-Hey, thanks.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.400
MIKE: Bada-bing.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.560
Oh, great.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.120
Hey, Ted, good morning.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:39.800
(CLUCKING)

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.880
See that, Mikey?
Ted's walking to work.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.800
Big deal.
Guy takes five steps and he's there.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:54.720
(PHONES RINGING)

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.640
FEMALE MONSTER:
Monsters, Inc. Please hold.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.360
-Mornin', Sulley.
-Mornin', Ricky.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.760
-It's the Sullster.
-See you on the scare floor.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.560
-Hey Marge. How was jury duty?
-Morning, Sulley.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:07.680
Hey.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.680
Hey. It's still leaning to the left.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.640
-It is not.
-Hey, fellas. Hey, Jerry.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.760
-Hey, Mr. Sullivan.
-Guys, I told you, call me Sulley.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.120
-I don't think so.
-We want to wish you good luck today.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.040
Hey, hey, get lost, you two.
You're making him lose his focus.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.960
-Sorry.
-See you later, fellas.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.720
Go get 'em, Mr. Sullivan.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.200
Quiet.
You're making him lose his focus.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.960
-Oh, no. Sorry!
-Shut up!

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.920
Monsters, Inc. Please hold.
Monsters, Inc. I'll connect you.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.080
Miss Fearmonger is on vacation.
Would you like her voicemail?

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.680
-Schmoopsie-pooh.
-Googly bear.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.280
-Happy birthday.
-Googly-woogly, you remembered.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.280
-Hey, Sulley-wulley.
-Hey, Celia-wheelia.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.960
-(CLEARS THROAT) Happy birthday.
-Thanks.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.280
So are we going
anywhere special tonight?

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.840
I just got us into a little place
called Harryhausen's.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:05.920
(GASPS)

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:09.160
Harryhausen's? But it's impossible
to get a reservation there.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.760
Not for googly bear.
I will see you at quittin' time.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.920
-Not a minute later.
-OK, sweetheart.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.800
Think romantical thoughts.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.280
♪ You and me
Me and you

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.360
♪ Both of us together ♪

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:24.840
You know, pal, she's the one.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.640
-That's it. She is the one.
-I'm happy for you.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.160
Thanks for hooking me up
with those reservations.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.320
They're under the name "googly bear."

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.400
Good...
You know, that wasn't very funny.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.480
(GASPS)

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.960
-What the...
-Wazowski.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.160
What do you know?

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.120
It scares little kids
and little monsters.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.720
I wasn't scared.
I have allergies.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:52.800
(COUGHS)

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:56.120
-Uh-huh. Sure.
-Randall, save it for the scare floor.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.920
I'm in the zone today, Sullivan.
Gonna do serious scaring.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.360
-Putting up some big numbers.
-Randall, that's great.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.680
That should make it more humiliating
when we break the record first. Ha, ha!

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.640
(SHUSHING)

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.720
Do you hear that?
It's the winds of change.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.520
(MOCKING VOICE) "You hear that?
It's the winds of..."

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.560
What a creep.
One of these days I am really

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.520
gonna let you
teach that guy a lesson.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.400
(DEEP CROAKING)

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.560
Chalooby. Baby.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.520
Good morning, Roz,
my succulent garden snail.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:41.000
-Who would we be scaring today?
-Wazowski.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.560
You didn't file your paperwork
last night.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.520
Oh, that darn paperwork.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.880
Wouldn't it be easier
if it all just blew away?

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.400
Don't let it happen again.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.960
Yes. Well, I'll try to be less careless.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.920
I'm watching you, Wazowski.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.920
Always watching.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.200
-She's nuts.
-ROZ: Always.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.480
CELIA ON PA:
All scare floors are now active.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.000
Assistants, please report
to your stations.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:21.880
(BELL DINGS)

